{
  "schema_version": "2.0",
  "id": "10332_kumanaku",
  "headword": "くまなく",
  "reading": "くまなく",
  "part_of_speech": "adverb",
  "gloss": "thoroughly; all over; every corner",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "thoroughly, all over, every corner",
      "explanation": "Without leaving any area unchecked or untouched. Describes searching, looking, or covering an area completely."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "10332_kumanaku_ex1",
      "japanese": "{部屋|へや}をくまなく{探|さが}した。",
      "english": "I searched every corner of the room.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "10332_kumanaku_ex2",
      "japanese": "{警察|けいさつ}が{山|やま}をくまなく{捜索|そうさく}している。",
      "english": "The police are searching the mountain thoroughly.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "10332_kumanaku_ex3",
      "japanese": "{太陽|たいよう}の{光|ひかり}が{部屋|へや}のすみずみまでくまなく{届|とど}いていた。",
      "english": "The sunlight reached every corner of the room.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Written as {隈|くま}なく. The kanji {隈|くま} means \"dark corner\" or \"nook,\" so the word literally means \"without dark corners\" — i.e., leaving no corner unchecked.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- くまなく{探|さが}す: to search every corner\n- くまなく{調|しら}べる: to examine thoroughly\n- くまなく{見|み}る: to look all over\n- くまなく{捜索|そうさく}する: to search exhaustively\n\nUSAGE: Often used with verbs of searching, inspecting, or covering an area. A somewhat literary word, more common in writing and formal speech than casual conversation.",
